  "body": "What happens: the 3D Pocket ladder (`crates/motion/src/machining3d/ladder.rs`) skips a level for two different reasons:\n\n- the target is empty (the part fills the silhouette at that plane);\n- the target is not empty, but the cutter-centre area after the erosion by the tool radius is empty (the open area is narrower than the tool).\n\nWhen no level cuts, both cases give the same refusal: \"nothing to cut: the model fills the pocket at every level\". In the second case the message is wrong. The user must change the tool or the boundary, not the model.\n\nEvidence: #1706. The sample `testdata/models/sample_ap214.step` as imported casts a strip 6.53 mm wide. A 6 mm end mill gets \"the model fills the pocket at every level\", but the part does not fill the strip. The refusal itself is correct.\n\nExpected: the refusal names the case. For example: \"nothing to cut: the open area is narrower than the 6 mm tool at every level\". The refusal stays a refusal.\n\nFound while working #1706.\n\nDone means: the ladder tells the two cases apart in its refusal text, and a test pins each text.\n",
